<p>I'm sorry about all of the things you didn't like.</p>
<p>In answer to your main concern about unclear narrative and repetition: the documents are meant to be unclear and ambiguous. I thought it helped to introduce the possibility that the anomaly was actively modifying the pages. The final note is meant to add the idea that the anomaly was sent both back in time, creating itself, as well as being sent into our universe. However, because that note was written after the spacecraft was destroyed, there's no way we would have it over in our universe, right?</p>
<p>To put it simply, none of this is just raw, unmodified documentation. The anomaly has changed and added things, perhaps in an effort to explain how it came to be, perhaps to narcissistically play itself up. It's all close, but not quite clear intentionally.</p>
<p>I hope you reconsider your position.</p>

