<p>I pretty much agree with this to be honest.</p>
<p>I also have a few issues with your extra docs, most specifically that there are a lot of cases where you mention that the anomaly DOESN'T do something, presumably because it will begin doing it later. For example, in the 2nd (I think) you say that it doesn't affect humans, but I had no reason to believe it did in the first place.</p>
<p>Also, you call this an infohazard and I'm not sure that is what this is. Infohazards are linked to objects and manifest their effect when you refer to it in someway (writing about it, thinking about it etc). Pretty sure this is a meme (spreads to other images on contact) or a cognitohazard (infects humans who look at them), or both.</p>
<p>Aaand yeah, I felt there was very little pay off for this. I think the end was trying to suggest that the rocket, or the hard drive from it at least, was shunted to the baseline Foundation reality from this alternate one? I dunno. Especially for a piece this long I feel like this level of ambiguity is pretty bad.</p>

							</div>

								
